  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "Long-read sequencing now yields near-complete assemblies of repetitive and structurally complex genomes, enabling pangenome and trait-level analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is long-read de novo assembly producing chromosome-level or near-complete genomes, from which structural and gene-content variation is then characterized. A chromosome-level assembly of the vascular plant Dracocephalum ruyschiana is reported. Optimized PacBio HiFi assembly recovers near-complete genomes of eight cloned Malian Plasmodium falciparum field isolates to reveal full genome architecture. A gene-based pangenome of 140 Caenorhabditis elegans strains identifies copy-number variation within hyper-divergent regions and a novel anthelmintic resistance locus. A chromosome-scale HiFi and Hi-C reference for invasive eastern mosquitofish, Gambusia holbrooki, reveals a newly evolved W/Z sex chromosome pair. What is new here is the application of assembly-first genomics across a plant, a parasite field-isolate set, a nematode pangenome and a vertebrate reference, with the resulting assemblies used to expose lineage-specific variation.",
